# 2.baseline

measure the clean baseline: build vs jest split, per-file cost, per-case verdicts.

.why-this-order = every later stone is judged against this number. a baseline taken
  after a change is not a baseline.

.guard = .log/bench.acceptance/before.json exists, holds a wallMs, and holds a case
  map with a verdict per case.

.hardwon = FREEZE THE TREE. jest lazy-loads each test file as it reaches it, so an
  edit to the harness mid-run is picked up by files not yet loaded. the first attempt
  was corrupted this way and had to be killed and redone. the measurement is an
  experiment; protect it like one.
